    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. one more thing, i've heard some people mention that with mutual funds, there are sometimes hidden issues or things that mess with the returns that you don't see immediately. can you explain if there are any common risks or \"glitches\" in how these funds operate or how their fees are structured?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A common issue with mutual funds is \"management style drift,\" where a fund manager gradually shifts away from the stated investment objective without notifying investors promptly. Their fees can also harbor hidden costs, such as high expense ratios or loads (sales charges) that erode returns without being immediately obvious. Additionally, active management can lead to higher turnover, incurring brokerage costs that are passed directly to the fund shareholder.",
      "source": "target",
